          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mrwyp87ysujuewva",
          "message": {
            "text": "Subject-line-only matching is the load-bearing choice (HS-9389 finding): commit BODIES in this repo routinely cross-reference other tickets (\"Follow-up from HS-9384\" in HS-9390's commit), and pulling those diffs into a ticket's review would be wrong. The word-boundary lookaround mirrors `prNotesReader`'s ticket matcher so `HS-12` never matches `HS-123`. Note the deliberate looseness WITHIN the subject: any word-boundary mention in a subject counts (not only the leading `HS-NNNN:` form), because squash/merge subjects sometimes carry the ref mid-line.\n",
            "markdown": "Subject-line-only matching is the load-bearing choice (HS-9389 finding): commit BODIES in this repo routinely cross-reference other tickets (\"Follow-up from HS-9384\" in HS-9390's commit), and pulling those diffs into a ticket's review would be wrong. The word-boundary lookaround mirrors `prNotesReader`'s ticket matcher so `HS-12` never matches `HS-123`. Note the deliberate looseness WITHIN the subject: any word-boundary mention in a subject counts (not only the leading `HS-NNNN:` form), because squash/merge subjects sometimes carry the ref mid-line.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/reviewNotes/ticketCommits.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 57,
                  "endLine": 66,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "\n/** Pure: the entries whose SUBJECT references the ticket (word-boundary). */\nexport function matchTicketCommits(entries: readonly CommitEntry[], ticketNumber: string): CommitEntry[] {\n  const re = ticketRefRegExp(ticketNumber);\n  return entries.filter(e => re.test(e.subject));\n}\n\n/**\n * Pure: cluster matched commits into linear groups. `entries` is the FULL bounded\n * log (newest first — its indexes are the history positions); `matched` must be a"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
